tersen, Anne Suhr","orcid":"0000-0002-2621-4360","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lonny","key":"stokholmpau","last":"Stokholm","locid":"ab6bde17-94c0-482d-bb34-495daa518640","name":"Stokholm, Lonny","orcid":"0000-0002-9727-6649","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","dansk oftalmologisk selskab","organization of danish ophthalmologists"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8d6b9352-1174-4cea-ab6e-2fbbc6ad990c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Diabetic retinopathy as an independent marker of cardiovascular disease in type 1 diabetes: results from a nationwide longitudinal matched case-cohort study.","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-766162","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Aim: This study aimed to investigate the short-and long-term effect on diabetic retinopathy (DR) in individuals with type 1 diabetes treated with continuous subcutaneous insulin injections (CSII) compared to those using multiple daily injections (MDI). Methods: We conducted a register-based matched cohort study utilizing data from the Danish Registry of Diabetic Retinopathy as well as several other national Danish health registers. Our cohort consisted of all individuals with type 1 diabetes who attended the Danish screening program for DR from 2013 to 2022. We included individuals registered with CSII treatment, and compared them to individuals using MDI, matched by age, sex, and DR level. Cox regression analysis was performed to evaluate the outcomes. Results: The study included 674 individuals treated with CSII and 2006 matched MDI users. In our cohort 53.4 % were female and median age was 36 (IQR 27–47). Average follow-up risk-time was 4.8 years. There was no difference in the risk of DR worsening between the CSII group and MDI group (HR 1.05 [95%CI 0.91; 1.22], p = 0.49). However, an increased risk of focal photocoagulation was observed in the CSII group (HR 2.40 [95%CI 1.11; 5.19], p = 0.03). Conclusions: Our findings indicate that CSII treatment does not confer a significant difference in the overall short- and long-term risk of DR worsening or ocular intervention compared to MDI treatment. These results provide insights into the DR outcomes of CSII treatment in individuals with type 1 diabetes.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Suhr Thykjær, Anne","Rosengaard, Louise","Andersen, Nis","Andresen, Jens","Hajari, Javad","Heegaard, Steffen","Højlund, Kurt","Kawasaki, Ryo","Laugesen, Caroline S.","Möller, Sören","Pedersen, Frederik Nørregaard","Schielke, Katja","Stokholm, Lonny","Grauslund, Jakob"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-755813"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Suhr Thykjær, Anne","Thykjær, Anne S."],"country":["Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Osaka University","The University of Osaka"],"keyword":["Adult","Cohort Studies","Continuous subcutaneous insulin injections","Denmark epidemiology","Diabetes Mellitus Type 1 complications","Diabetic Retinopathy epidemiology","Diabetic retinopathy","Female","Humans","Hypoglycemic Agents administration dosage","Incidence","Injections Subcutaneous","Insulin Infusion Systems","Insulin administration dosage","Long term","Male","Middle Aged","Multiple daily injections","Progression","Registries"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of continuous subcutaneous insulin therapy and diabetic retinopathy in type 000000000001 diabetes a national cohort study","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jdiacomp.2024.108830","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding: The completion of this study was possible due to the funding of VELUX Foundations (grant number 00028744), Steno Diabetes Center Odense and the M.L. J\\u00F8rgensen and Gunnar Hansen foundation. The study funders were not involved in any part of the study design, the collection, analysis or interpretation of data, nor were they involved in writing the manuscript. No restrictions were made regarding publication."],"id":"S02-100.00-755813","identifier":[{"id":"39096767","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85200159803","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-58af7676-fd89-41f8-9e37-0529b8201f69","sd