:9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Ryo","key":"kawasakipau","last":"Kawasaki","locid":"9b782ced-ac4a-44d9-848c-d60a6e110229","name":"Kawasaki, Ryo","orcid":"0000-0002-7492-6303","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kurt","key":"højlundpau","last":"Højlund","locid":"de11c7e6-25a6-4e23-95bb-fe86d3d775ab","name":"Højlund, Kurt","orcid":"0000-0002-0891-4224","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Hass","key":"rubinpau","last":"Rubin","locid":"90ded8f7-7d96-472a-8305-1bdb7bf0d345","name":"Rubin, Katrine Hass","orcid":"0000-0001-5045-536X","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lonny","key":"stokholmpau","last":"Stokholm","locid":"ab6bde17-94c0-482d-bb34-495daa518640","name":"Stokholm, Lonny","orcid":"0000-0002-9727-6649","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Tunde","key":"petopau","last":"Peto","name":"Peto, Tunde","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob","key":"grauslundpau","last":"Grauslund","locid":"72447336-2d4c-44a2-b4a5-f99df775a980","name":"Grauslund, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0001-5019-0736","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37066883"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aos.15667","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"7","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"783-788","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"101"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153227524"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","organization of danish ophthalmologists","organization of danish practicing ophthalmologists"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1df8b825-7d5d-447c-b8f6-f707b6b77db3","ku-8f578f59-f49f-41b2-9c6a-e09dbaf3a3eb","sdu-36e638ee-1efe-4397-8b45-efe4d13e4367"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Inter-grader reliability in the Danish screening programme for diabetic retinopathy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.17-715887","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To evaluate the proliferative diabetic retinopathy (PDR) progression rates and identify the demographic and clinical characteristics of patients who later developed PDR compared with patients who did not progress to that state. DESIGN: A national 5-year register-based cohort study including 201 945 patients with diabetes. SUBJECTS: Patients with diabetes who had attended the Danish national screening program (2013-2018) for diabetic retinopathy (DR). METHODS: We used the first screening episode as the index date and included both eyes of patients with and without subsequent progression of PDR. Data were linked with various national health registries to investigate relevant clinical and demographic parameters. The International Clinical Retinopathy Disease Scale was used to classify DR, with no DR as level 0, mild DR as level 1, moderate DR as level 2, severe DR as level 3, and PDR as level 4. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES: Hazard ratios (HRs) for incident PDR for all relevant demographic and clinical parameters and 1-, 3-, and 5-year incidence rates of PDR according to baseline DR level. RESULTS: Progression to PDR within 5 years was identified in 2384 eyes of 1780 patients. Proliferative diabetic retinopathy progression rates from baseline DR level 3 at 1, 3 and 5 years were 3.6%, 10.9%, and 14.7%, respectively. The median number of visits was 3 (interquartile range, 1-4). Progression to PDR was predicted in a multivariable model by duration of diabetes (HR, 4.66 per 10 years; 95% confidence interval [CI], 4.05-5.37), type 1 diabetes (HR, 9.61; 95% CI, 8.01-11.53), a Charlson Comorbidity Index score of > 0 (score 1: HR, 4.62; 95% CI, 4.14-5.15; score 2: HR, 2.28; 95% CI, 1.90-2.74; score ≥ 3: HR, 4.28; 95% CI, 3.54-5.17), use of insulin (HR, 5.33; 95% CI, 4.49-6.33), and use of antihypertensive medications (HR, 2.23; 95% CI, 1.90-2.61). CONCLUSIONS: In a 5-year longitudinal study of an entire screening nation, we found increased risk of PDR with increasing baseline DR levels, longer duration of diabetes, type 1 diabetes, systemic comorbidity, use of insulin, and blood pressure-lowering medications. Most interestingly, we found lower risk of progression from DR level 3 to PDR compared with that in previous studies. FINANCIAL DISCLOSURES: Proprietary or commercial disclosure may be found after the references.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Dinesen, Sebastian","Stokholm, Lonny","Subhi, Yousif","Peto, Tunde","Savarimuthu, Thiusius Rajeeth","Andersen, Nis","Andresen, Jens","Bek, Toke","Hajari, Javad","Heegaard, Steffen","Højlund, Kurt","Laugesen, Caroline Schmidt","Kawasaki, Ryo","Möller, Sören","Schielke, Katja","Suhr Thykjær, Anne","Pedersen, Frederik Nørregaard","Grauslund, Jakob"],"cuid":["S04-099.92-691746"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Dinesen, Sebastian"],"country":["Japan","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Osaka University","Queen's University Belfast","The University of Osaka","University of Osaka"],"keyword":["Epidemiology","Proliferative diabetic retinopathy","Risk factor"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Danish Ophthalmological Society"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"five year incidence of proliferative diabetic retinopathy and associated risk factors in a nationwide cohort of 000000000201 000000000945 danish patients with diabetes","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.xops.2023.100291","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Supported by Steno Diabetes Center Odense, Odense, Denmark, and the Region of Southern Denmark, Denmark. The funding organizations had no role in the design or conduct of this research. The authors have made the following disclosures: R.K.: Grant – Topcon, Senju, Novartis, Nanolux, Tamron, and WHILL, outside the submitted work; Personal fees – Novartis, Bayer, Office Future, Nanolux, Kowa, Santen, and Bausch Lomb, outside the submitted work.J.G.: Grant – VELUX FONDEN; Personal fees – Bayer, Novartis, Roche, Allergan, and Santen, outside the submitted work."],"id":"S04-099.92-691746","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10070897","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37025947","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85151457296","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5f1e0ac4-c784-468e-8ce1-6bc28d33365b","au-35752031-d2bd-4aa5-a618-871d14340700","ku-1242160d-cbe8-4051-82cb-10d362738c25","sdu-2683cd26-dc56-42fc-9b7e-410675d940ef"],"keyword":["Epidemiology","Proliferative diabetic retinopathy","risk factor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-124A7C5721CB68D5910A1B8C90510700"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/226220866/Five_Year_Incidence_of_Proliferative_Di...pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/367911623/1_s2.0_S2666914523000234_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.xops.2023.100291","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/550320632/PIIS2666914523000234.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U",