","status":"p","title":"Ophthalmology Science","title_org":"Ophthalmology science","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151457296"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","organization of danish ophthalmologists","organization of danish practicing ophthalmologists"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5f1e0ac4-c784-468e-8ce1-6bc28d33365b","au-35752031-d2bd-4aa5-a618-871d14340700","ku-1242160d-cbe8-4051-82cb-10d362738c25","sdu-2683cd26-dc56-42fc-9b7e-410675d940ef"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Five-Year Incidence of Proliferative Diabetic Retinopathy and Associated Risk Factors in a Nationwide Cohort of 201 945 Danish Patients with Diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.92-691746","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Aims Bariatric surgery is used to induce weight loss and glycemic stability in type 2 diabetes (T2D). It has been a concern that this may lead to early worsening of diabetic retinopathy (DR) due to a rapid decline in HbA1c. In this study, we evaluated the risk of short and long-term DR development and need for ocular intervention in an entire nation of individuals with T2D undergoing bariatric surgery. Methods The study comprised a national, register-based cohort of individuals with T2D screened for DR. Cases were matched by age, sex and DR level at the date of surgery (index date) with non-bariatric controls. We extracted information on DR levels, in- and outpatient treatments, pharmaceutical prescriptions and laboratory values. We evaluated worsening of DR (incident and progressive DR) at follow-up (6 and 36 months). Results Amongst 238,967 individuals with T2D, who attended diabetic eye screening, we identified 553 that underwent bariatric surgery (0.2%) and 2677 non-bariatric controls. Median age was 49 years, and 63% were female. Cases had more comorbidities, lower HbA1c as well as more frequent use of glucose-lowering and antihypertensive medication than controls at index date. In a fully adjusted logistic regression model, the risk of DR worsening for cases was not significantly different compared to controls, neither short-term (OR 0.41 [CI 95% 0.13; 1.33], p = 0.14) nor long-term (OR 0.64 [CI 95% 0.33; 1.24], p = 0.18). Conclusions In this nationwide study, bariatric surgery did not associate with increased risk of short- or long-term DR worsening.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Thykjær, Anne S.","Rosengaard, Louise","Andersen, Nis","Andresen, Jens","Bek, Toke","Hajari, Javad","Heegaard, Steffen","Højlund, Kurt","Kawasaki, Ryo","Laugesen, Caroline S.","Möller, Sören","Pedersen, Frederik N.","Schielke, Katja Christina","Stokholm, Lonny","Grauslund, Jakob"],"cuid":["S04-099.92-715741"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Suhr Thykjær, Anne","Thykjær, Anne S."],"country":["Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Osaka University","The University of Osaka"],"keyword":["Bariatric Surgery adverse effects","Bariatric surgery","Cohort Studies","Diabetes","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 complications","Diabetic Retinopathy epidemiology","Diabetic retinopathy","Epidemiology","Female","Glycated Hemoglobin","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Nationwide","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bariatric surgery in individuals with type 000000000002 diabetes is not associated with short or long term risk of diabetic retinopathy progression results from a nationwide cohort study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00592-023-02140-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-099.92-715741","identifier":[{"id":"37421439","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85164102067","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10520211","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-a012c956-f8a5-4d6e-9b0e-6c8cb098e507","au-f3fb2c97-1d67-41ef-9e13-a0245bf4cdee","ku-e972f89c-21b5-421c-beff-eabb8cc052e8","sdu-26ebe0d8-9ba2-4c35-b314-e83ece0f02e0"],"keyword":["Bariatric Surgery/adverse effects","Bariatric surgery","Cohort Studies","Diabetes","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/complications","Diabetic Retinopathy/epidemiology","Diabetic retinopathy","Epidemiology","Female","Glycated Hemoglob