rtal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-602475","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In composing multi-thematic questionnaires for the Lolland-Falster Health Study (LOFUS), we faced a range of challenges, for which we found limited guidance in the literature. LOFUS is a household-based population study covering multiple medical and social research areas and targeting the mixed rural-provincial population of 103,000 persons on the Danish islands Lolland and Falster. Households were randomly selected for invitation. In this paper, we describe and discuss challenges in developing the questionnaires related to stakeholders, content of the questionnaire, and the process itself. The development process was characterised by loops of learning and can be described as an iterative and incremental process. We propose recommendations to researchers and administrators involved in similar development processes, including awareness of the non-linearity and complexity of the process, a need for negotiations and navigation among multiple stakeholders, and acknowledgement of pragmatism as an inherent part of decisions made in the process.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Egholm, Cecilie Lindström","Packness, Aake","Stokholm, Jakob","Rasmussen, Knud","Ellervik, Christina","Simonsen, Erik","Christensen, Anne Illemann","Jepsen, Randi"],"cuid":["S02-087.94-041540"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Boston Children's Hospital","Harvard Medical School"],"keyword":["Items","Iterative and incremental process","LOFUS","Lolland Falster Health Study","Loops of learning","Population study","Questionnaire development","Questionnaires","Scales"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["National Institute of Public Health"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"questionnaire development for the lolland falster health study denmark an iterative and incremental process","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12874-020-00931-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.94-041540","identifier":[{"id":"32126988","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7055066","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85081042872","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-38aa7023-b951-41f5-8a1b-3fa703defbf5","sdu-de328a69-43f9-4f9e-86cc-277ca319ca24"],"keyword":["Items","Iterative and incremental process","LOFUS","Lolland-Falster Health study","Loops of learning","Population study","Questionnaire development","Questionnaires","Scales"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-61FBD4AC4D08FC0469F58AB9106F08CD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/243197995/Questionnaire_development_for_the_Lolland_Falster_Health_Study_Denmark.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/168604407/s12874_020_00931_1_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12874-020-00931-1","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Nykøbing Falster Sygehus","Region Sjælland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universitie