{"abstract":"I almindelighed er det forældres opgave i samarbejde med professionelle at bakke op om deres børns hverdagsliv i skole og fritid. Når børn er bosat udenfor eget hjem, påtager ”samfundet” sig en større eller mindre del af disse forældreopgaver, og den varetages af forskellige fagpersoner i et tværprofessionelt samarbejde. Forskning har peget på, at børn og unge bosat udenfor eget hjem forlader skolen med ringere skolefærdigheder end andre børn, og at det har betydning for deres fremtidige uddannelsesmuligheder. Artiklen tager udgangspunkt i et forskningsprojekt, der har fulgt det tværprofessionelle samarbejde om at understøtte børns skolegang og fritidsliv under deres anbringelser. Artiklen bidrager med viden om, hvordan vanskeligheder i disse børns hverdagsliv er forbundet med problemer i det tværprofessionelle samarbejde. Diskussioner om omsorg for disse børn handler ofte om, hvorvidt børnene har brug for særlige hensyn, eller om voksne i stedet bør stille flere krav. Artiklen peger på, at hensyn og krav må forstås situeret og som indbyrdes forbundne aspekter ved omsorg for børn. Desuden diskuteres det, hvordan kommunale bestræbelser på at sætte klare mål og uddelegere omsorgsopgaver på anbringelsesområdet skaber betingelser for det tværprofessionelle samarbejde om at udvikle fælles handlemuligheder.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Schwartz, Ida","Hansen, Anne Boye","Stokholm, Gitte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-647249"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anbringelse uden for hjemmet","Børn","Hverdagsliv","Samarbejde"],"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tværprofessionelt samarbejde om børneliv i vanskeligheder","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-647249","ids":["ucl-35102d5b-a5e4-4555-9564-1482828db1dc"],"keyword":["anbringelse uden for hjemmet","børn","hverdagsliv","samarbejde"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-A53C1B561D854CD23026A4B5C4F22FF3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Kompetence- og Organisationsudvikling, Anvendt Velfærdsforskning"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida","key":"schwartzpau","last":"Schwartz","locid":"11d654e2-60cf-4ef8-9e6c-7562ec17b278","name":"Schwartz, Ida","orcid":"0000-0001-9001-7911","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Boye","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"238d32a2-52a5-4783-8e21-3758a0e82689","name":"Hansen, Anne Boye","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte","key":"stokholmpau","last":"Stokholm","locid":"65a7688c-05a3-402f-8c97-7e754678b30b","name":"Stokholm, Gitte","orcid":"0000-0003-2577-3854","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["13963953"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nordiske Udkast","pages":"37-61","paperid":"1","status":"p","title":"Nordiske Udkast","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucl-35102d5b-a5e4-4555-9564-1482828db1dc"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"Tværprofessionelt samarbejde om børneliv i vanskeligheder","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-647249","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Pregnant women were suspected to be at particular risk when H1N1pnd09 influenza became pandemic in 2009. Our primary objective was to compare the immune responses conferred by MF59®-adjuvanted vaccine (Focetria®) in H1N1pnd09-naïve pregnant and non-pregnant women. The secondary aims were to compare influences of dose and adjuvant on the immune response. METHODS: The study was nested in the Copenhagen Prospective Studies on Asthma in Childhood (COPSAC2010) pregnancy cohort in 2009-2010 and conducted as a single-blinded block-randomised [1∶1∶1] controlled clinical trial in pregnant women after gestational week 20: (1) 7.5 µg H1N1pnd09 antigen with MF59-adjuvant (Pa7.5 µg); (2) 3.75 µg antigen half MF59-adjuvanted (Pa3.75 µg); (3) 15 µg antigen unadjuvanted (P15 µg); and in non-pregnant women receiving (4) 7.5 µg antigen full adjuvanted (NPa7.5 µg). Blood samples were collected at baseline, 3 weeks, 3 and 10 months after vaccination, adverse events were recorded prospectively. RESULTS: 58 pregnant women were allocated to Pa7.5 µg and 149 non-pregnant women were recruited to NPa7.5 µg. The sero-conversion rate was significantly increased in non-pregnant (NPa7.5 µg) compared with pregnant (Pa7.5 µg) women (OR = 2.48 [1.03-5.95], p = 0.04) and geometric mean titers trended towards being higher, but this difference was not statistically significant (ratio 1.27 [0.85-1.93], p = 0.23). The significant titer increase rate showed no difference between pregnant (Pa7.5 µg) and non-pregnant (NPa7.5 µg) groups (OR = 0.49 [0.13-1.85], p = 0.29). CONCLUSION: Our study suggests the immune response to the 7.5 µg MF59-adjuvanted Focetria® H1N1pnd09 vaccine in pregnant women may be diminished compared with non-pregnant women. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov NCT01012557.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bischoff, Anne Louise","Følsgaard, Nilofar Vahman","Carson, Charlotte Giwercman","Stokholm, Jakob","Pedersen, Louise","Holmberg, Maria","Bisgaard, Amalie","Birch, Sune","Tsai, Theodore F","Bisgaard, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-488575"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adjuvants Immunologic","Adult","Female","Humans","Influenza A Virus H1N1 Subtype","Influenza Human","Influenza Vaccines","Polysorbates","Pregnancy","Pregnancy Complications Infectious","Prospective Studies","Seroepidemiologic Studies","Squalene","Vaccination"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"altered response to a h000000000001n000000000001 pnd000000000009 vaccination in pregnant women a single blinded randomized controlled trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0056700","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-488575","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3630160","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23637733","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84876341732","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9f2ed1cb-86dc-414c-917b-a0b3e1a7301e"],"keyword":["Adjuvants, Immunologic","Adult","Female","Humans","Influenza A Virus, H1N1 Subtype","Influenza Vaccines","Influenza, Human","Polysorbates","Pregnancy","Pregnancy Complications, Infectious","Prospective Studies","Seroepidemiologic Studies","Squalene","Vaccination"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3D03C891A5F8726B6AFE7427FDF84A40"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0056700","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/261450409/Altered_Response_to_A_H1N1_pnd09_Vaccination_in_Pregnant_Women.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Louise","key":"bischoffannelouisepau","last":"Bischoff","locid":"62cf0bce-635c-4e11-93dd-f2d6e7c72da8","name":"Bischoff, Anne Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nilofar Vahman","key":"følsgaardnilofarvahmanpau","last":"Følsgaard","locid":"0043be1c-2ec2-4cd9-99f2-e3c91ae15239","name":"Følsgaard, Nilofar Vahman","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte Giwercman","key":"carsoncharlottegiwercmanpau","last":"Carson","name":"Carson, Charlotte Giwercman","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jakob","key":"stokholmjakobpau","last":"Stokholm","name":"Stokholm, Jakob","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"pedersenlouisepau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Louise","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Maria","key":"holmbergmariapau","last":"Holmberg","name":"Holmberg, Maria","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Amalie","key":"bisgaardamaliepau","last":"Bisgaard","name":"Bisgaard, Amalie","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sune","key":"birchsunepau","last":"Birch","name":"Birch, Sune","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Theodore F","key":"tsaitheodorefpau","last":"Tsai","name":"Tsai, Theodore F","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hans","key":"bisgaardhanspau","last":"Bisgaard","locid":"6ee3c769-8284-4a60-a3aa-1282019f8e80","name":"Bisgaard, Hans","orcid":"0000-0003-4131-7592","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23637733"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0056700","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"4","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e56700","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84876341732"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9f2ed1cb-86dc-414c-917b-a0b3e1a7301e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Altered Response to A(H1N1)pnd09 Vaccination in Pregnant Women : A Single Blinded Randomized Controlled Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-488575","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"author_count":11,"contributors":["Stokholm, Jakob","Schjørring, Susanne","Pedersen, Louise Lindkvist","Bischoff, Anne Louise","Følsgaard, Nilofar Vahman","Carson, Charlotte G","Chawes, Bo","Bønnelykke, Klaus","Mølgaard, Anne","Krogfelt, Karen","Bisgaard, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-471605"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence and predictors of antibiotic administration during pregnancy and birth","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0082932","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-471605","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3858309","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"24340068","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84892400186","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-82a8417b-48b9-4cea-b931-7d405daf9181"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E7F17F988D93FB68EF8E8DA656BE44BD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0082932","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Næstved, Slagelse and Ringsted"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Gynaecology, Obstetrics and Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jakob","key":"stokholmpau","last":"Stokholm","name":"Stokholm, Jakob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Susanne","key":"schjørringpau","last":"Schjørring","name":"Schjørring, Susanne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"5287771a-90ad-43b2-a994-0b1688bcf51c","name":"Pedersen, Louise Lindkvist","name_org":"Pedersen, Louise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne Louise","key":"bischoffpau","last":"Bischoff","locid":"62cf0bce-635c-4e11-93dd-f2d6e7c72da8","name":"Bischoff, Anne Louise","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nilofar","key":"følsgaardpau","last":"Følsgaard","locid":"0043be1c-2ec2-4cd9-99f2-e3c91ae15239","name":"Følsgaard, Nilofar Vahman","name_org":"Følsgaard, Nilofar","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte G","key":"carsonpau","last":"Carson","name":"Carson, Charlotte G","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bo L K","key":"chawespau","last":"Chawes","locid":"a43d3bab-d625-4981-a8aa-d58d4b4a8b75","name":"Chawes, Bo","name_org":"Chawes, Bo L K","orcid":"0000-0001-6846-6243","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus","key":"bønnelykkepau","last":"Bønnelykke","locid":"c36b6936-2cc4-41b1-b7c5-a97978afe417","name":"Bønnelykke, Klaus","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne","key":"mølgaardpau","last":"Mølgaard","locid":"18764581-0232-4aa6-be20-d722550f2651","name":"Mølgaard, Anne","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Karen","key":"krogfeltpau","last":"Krogfelt","name":"Krogfelt, Karen","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Hans","key":"bisgaardpau","last":"Bisgaard","locid":"6ee3c769-8284-4a60-a3aa-1282019f8e80","name":"Bisgaard, Hans","orcid":"0000-0003-4131-7592","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24340068"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0082932","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"12","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e82932","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84892400186"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-82a8417b-48b9-4cea-b931-7d405daf9181"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prevalence and Predictors of Antibiotic Administration during Pregnancy and Birth","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-471605","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We hypothesize that perinatal exposures, in particular the human microbiome and maternal nutrition during pregnancy, interact with the genetic predisposition to cause an abnormal immune modulation in early life towards a trajectory to chronic inflammatory diseases such as asthma and others. The aim of this study is to explore these interactions by conducting a longitudinal study in an unselected cohort of pregnant women and their offspring with emphasis on deep clinical phenotyping, exposure assessment, and biobanking. Exposure assessments focus on the human microbiome. Nutritional intervention during pregnancy in randomized controlled trials are included in the study to prevent disease and to be able to establish causal relationships. Pregnant women from eastern Denmark were invited during 2008–2010 to a novel unselected ‘COPSAC2010’ cohort. The women visited the clinic during pregnancy weeks 24 and 36. Their children were followed at the clinic with deep phenotyping and collection of biological samples at nine regular visits until the age of 3 and at acute symptoms. Randomized controlled trials of high‐dose vitamin D and fish oil supplements were conducted during pregnancy, and a trial of azithromycin for acute lung symptoms was conducted in the children with recurrent wheeze. Seven hundred and thirty‐eight mothers were recruited from week 24 of gestation, and 700 of their children were included in the birth cohort. The cohort has an over‐representation of atopic parents. The participant satisfaction was high and the adherence equally high with 685 children (98%) attending the 1 year clinic visit and 667 children (95%) attending the 2 year clinic visit. The COPSAC2010 birth cohort study provides longitudinal clinical follow‐up with highly specific end‐points, exposure assessments, and biobanking. The cohort has a high adherence rate promising strong data to elucidate the interaction between genomics and the exposome in perinatal life leading to lifestyle‐related chronic inflammatory disorders such as asthma.","author_count":32,"contributors":["Bisgaard, Hans Flinker","Vissing, Nadja Hawwa","Carson, C. G.","Bischoff, Anne Louise","Følsgaard, Nilofar Vahman","Kreiner‐Møller, E.","Chawes, Bo Lund Krogsgaard","Stokholm, J.","Pedersen, L.","Bjarnadóttir, E.","Thysen, Anna Hammerich","Nilsson, E.","Mortensen, L. J.","Olsen, S. F.","Schjørring, S.","Krogfelt, Karen Angeliki","Lauritzen, L.","Brix, Susanne","Bønnelykke, K."],"cuid":["S02-092.02-035006"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep phenotyping of the unselected copsac000000002010 birth cohort study","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/65978022/cea12213.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.02-035006","identifier":[{"id":"84892392750","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24118234","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4158856","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-68fc5e1b-a416-450d-83bf-9f42c972f41f","ku-8a547169-6acb-4242-991b-e8b85f146387"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5540F0F492E5ADF97C3BEC15D32C3231"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cea.12213","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/65978022/cea12213.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","ke