{"abstract":"Furred pets in the household are known reservoirs for pathogenic bacteria, but it is not known if transmission of bacteria between pet and owner leads to significantly increased rate of infections. We studied whether cats and dogs living in the household of pregnant women affect the commensal vaginal flora, and furthermore the need for oral antibiotics and rate of urinary tract infections during pregnancy.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Stokholm, Jakob","Schjørring, Susanne","Pedersen, Louise","Bischoff, Anne Louise","Følsgaard, Nilofar","Carson, Charlotte G","Chawes, Bo","Bønnelykke, Klaus","Mølgaard, Anne","Krogfelt, Karen","Bisgaard, Hans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-526710"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"living with cat and dog increases vaginal colonization with e coli in pregnant women","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0046226","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-526710","identifier":[{"id":"23049986","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84866660590","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3458003","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-df2060e2-1125-481e-b89c-0acfac89ee5e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1C891231C8155D8FD9815C7106B4D0AA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0046226","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/261451153/Living_with_Cat_and_Dog_Increases_Vaginal_Colonizationwith_E._coli_in_Pregnant_Women.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Næstved, Slagelse and Ringsted"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Department of Systems Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Gynaecology, Obstetrics and Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob","key":"stokholmpau","last":"Stokholm","name":"Stokholm, Jakob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Susanne","key":"schjørringpau","last":"Schjørring","name":"Schjørring, Susanne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Louise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne Louise","key":"bischoffpau","last":"Bischoff","name":"Bischoff, Anne Louise","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nilofar","key":"følsgaardpau","last":"Følsgaard","name":"Følsgaard, Nilofar","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte G","key":"carsonpau","last":"Carson","name":"Carson, Charlotte G","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bo","key":"chawespau","last":"Chawes","name":"Chawes, Bo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Klaus","key":"bønnelykkepau","last":"Bønnelykke","name":"Bønnelykke, Klaus","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne","key":"mølgaardpau","last":"Mølgaard","name":"Mølgaard, Anne","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Karen","key":"krogfeltpau","last":"Krogfelt","name":"Krogfelt, Karen","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Hans","key":"bisgaardpau","last":"Bisgaard","locid":"6ee3c769-8284-4a60-a3aa-1282019f8e80","name":"Bisgaard, Hans","orcid":"0000-0003-4131-7592","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23049986"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0046226","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"9","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e46226","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84866660590"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-df2060e2-1125-481e-b89c-0acfac89ee5e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Living with Cat and Dog Increases Vaginal Colonization with E. coli in Pregnant Women","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-526710","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Rationale: Heredity from mother or father may impact differently in complex diseases, such as atopy. Maternal atopy is a stronger risk factor than paternal atopy for the development of atopy in the offspring. We hypothesized that mother's and father's atopy would have a differential imprinting on the cytokines and chemokines in the upper airway mucosal lining fluid of healthy neonates. Objectives: To study parental atopic imprinting on the cytokines and chemokines in the upper airway mucosal lining fluid of healthy neonates. Methods: Eighteen cytokines and chemokines were quantified in nasal mucosal lining fluid in 309 neonates from the novel unselected Copenhagen Prospective Study on Asthma in Childhood (COPSAC) birth cohort. Measurements and Main Results: Maternal, but not paternal, atopic status (asthma, hay fever, or eczema with or without sensitization) was associated with general down-regulation of all 18 mediators assessed by principal component analysis (overall P = 0.015). Conclusions: Maternal atopy, but not paternal atopy, showed a strong linkage with a suppressed mucosal cytokine and chemokine signature in asymptomatic neonates, suggesting imprinting by the maternal milieu in utero or perinatal life.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Folsgaard, Nilofar V.","Chawes, Bo L.","Rasmussen, Morten A.","Bischoff, Anne L.","Carson, Charlotte G.","Stokholm, Jakob","Pedersen, Louise","Hansel, Trevor T.","Bonnelykke, Klaus","Brix, Susanne","Bisgaard, Hans"],"cuid":["S02-093.82-034030"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["